Enforce browser-conflict keybinding filtering on iOS

On iPadOS, WKWebView exposes navigator.keyboard causing BrowserFeatures
to report FullScreen keyboard support. This causes _assertBrowserConflicts
to skip all filtering, since it assumes fullscreen mode means system
shortcuts are available. But iOS still reserves Cmd+Space, Cmd+H, and
Cmd+Tab at the system level — VS Code never sees them, yet keybindings
bound to those combos would silently fail.

Always enforce the browser-conflict filter on iOS regardless of the
KeyboardSupport level. This matches what the filter already does in
non-iOS web contexts (it blocks Cmd+Arrow and Cmd+Digit to prevent
browser chrome from intercepting them).

